Ramos Castillo Abogados acts in administrative and constitutional disputes that affect the continuity, use, development and protection of real estate assets. Our work is particularly focused on disputes arising from administrative decrees, land-use and environmental restrictions, development permissions, expropriation measures, property-boundary questions and public-authority intervention affecting projects and privately held land.

We represent developers, industrial-project sponsors, real estate companies, civil associations and private property owners. Our recent work includes protecting the urbanisation of El Cielo Country Club against protected-area decrees; obtaining a definitive suspension in an expropriation dispute affecting the 207.5306-hectare Durango Logistics and Industrial Center; securing precautionary relief to allow construction processes and authorised operations to continue at an agro-industrial tequila production plant; and representing clients in disputes concerning alleged administrative takings, property boundaries and residential real estate regulation.

Founding partner José Pablo Ramos Castillo leads the firm’s real estate contentious work. He is supported by lawyers across the team on matters involving amparo proceedings, nullity actions, expert evidence on real estate identification, administrative strategy and urgent interim relief. The practice is distinguished by its focus on the legal protection of real estate projects and property rights when public measures threaten development, access, possession, use or continuity of operations.

