Ramos Castillo Abogados represents DURANPARK in an indirect amparo challenging an expropriation decree affecting the Durango Logistics and Industrial Center, a 207.5306-hectare property. The client’s attempt to register its public deed was refused after the Public Registry stated that the properties had been expropriated under Decree CCXXXIX.

The firm reviewed the client’s documentation and its arrangements with state authorities, developed the legal strategy and filed the constitutional challenge together with an application for suspension. A District Court granted a definitive suspension preventing action affecting the property and possession of the real estate, as well as administrative or registration actions related to the expropriation decree. The constitutional hearing remains pending. José Pablo Ramos Castillo leads the matter, supported by Daniel Rocha Peña and Héctor Alejandro Sánchez Carrera. The reported matter value is MXN 698,400,750.00.
